From 6e301753cd41d88cfba1b2075e7ec20aa00488ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gbolahan <gbolahanabiodun92@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:57:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix WhatsApp verification bypass, harden webhook, repair
 build and tests

Security (reproduced against the real migrations before fixing):
- Users could mark their own number verified by UPDATE on email_preferences,
  or by calling the SECURITY DEFINER RPCs with a hash of their choosing, on
  any user id, as anon. New migration 20261013000004 makes the verification
  columns server-only (trigger, INSERT and UPDATE), replaces the RPCs with
  service-role-only versions bound to the phone number, adds one verified
  owner per number, per-user and per-number rate limits, a STOP opt-out
  table, and resets previously "verified" rows.
- Webhook now fails closed (no secret or token = 500, no default token), uses
  the service-role client, dedupes atomically, processes whole batches,
  matches by digits, and records the inbound message that starts Meta's
  24-hour window. Cron uses that timestamp, not our last send.
- Verification UI added to Settings; phone numbers are normalised on save;
  the test-send action now requires a verified number.
- item_needs_washing no longer leaks other users' item state.

Build and tests:
- tests/db harness had no service_role, so a try/catch silently skipped the
  whole RLS suite. Harness fixed (service_role, Supabase default privileges)
  and the try/catch removed.
- Vitest now also runs src/**/*.test.ts; fixed 17 failing tests (mock chain,
  stale expectations, fetch mock leakage); owned-item matching now covers all
  categories except documents.
- 23 new DB attack tests and 14 webhook tests; docs updated.

